---
// The CV. The <article> below is a verbatim copy of the accepted CV in the Lucy repository
// (work-394, cv/cv.html), so a later revision of that CV is applied by pasting its <article> here.
import EngineeringLayout from "../layouts/EngineeringLayout.astro";
---

<EngineeringLayout
  title="CV - Rei Nuttanon"
  description="The CV of Rei Nuttanon, senior full-stack engineer: AI integration and agent governance, experience, open source and skills."
  page="cv"
  tone="paper"
  bodyClass="paper"
>
  <section class="paper cv-page" data-tone="paper">
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="rail"><p class="label">CV</p><p class="small faint note">Prints to A4. Choose “Save as PDF” in the print dialog.</p></div>
      <article class="body cv">
      <div class="cv-actions"><span class="small faint">Updated October 2026</span><button type="button" data-print>Download as PDF</button></div>
      <header class="cv-head">
        <h1>Rei Nuttanon</h1>
        <p class="role">Senior Full-Stack Engineer. AI integration and agent governance.</p>
        <p class="contact-line"><a href="mailto:reinuttanon@gmail.com">reinuttanon@gmail.com</a><a href="https://reinatt.com">reinatt.com</a><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/reinuttanon/">linkedin.com/in/reinuttanon</a><span>Bangkok, Thailand (UTC+7)</span></p>
        <p class="cv-avail">Open to relocation and remote work.</p>
      </header>
      <section class="cv-block"><p class="label">Summary</p><p class="summary">Built software professionally since 2011, across the full stack. Now building production software with AI agents, and designing the AI-governance architecture around them. Nearly 9 years in online payments and e-commerce. I translate my years of experience into AI agents and build the AI workflow that can ship things to production.</p><p class="summary">Lately, I’ve been diving into AI solutions that solve business challenges. Work that creates a big impact and changes lives is rewarding.</p></section>
      <section class="cv-block"><p class="label">Experience</p><div class="cv-track"><p class="cv-track-name">Career track</p><div class="cv-role"><div class="r1"><h3>Independent Software and Business Consultant</h3><span class="when">Jan 2025 - Present</span></div><div class="where">Bangkok, Thailand / remote</div><ul><li>Work with business owners to remove manual operations with tech/AI solutions. Initiate ideas, redesign operations, develop, integrate tech solutions, and get the team on board.</li></ul><div class="cv-sub"><div class="r1"><h4>Online marketing operations platform</h4><span class="when">Jan 2025 - Present</span></div><ul><li>Designed and built the platform for agencies and media buyers: a back office and tools for its operators, a customer app that runs inside LINE (LIFF) and on the web, and the API behind them.</li><li>Built the wallet and billing core: a prepaid wallet on a replayable ledger, with bank-transfer top-ups, usage charges, reversals and a reconciliation import.</li><li>Built the affiliate program: referral commissions earned on paid top-ups, settled monthly, then paid out or converted to credit.</li><li>Built internal tools to automate daily data reconciliation and operations. We saved hours by reducing manual tasks.</li><li>Laravel 11-13, PHP 8.2-8.4, PostgreSQL, Nuxt 4, Vue 3, TypeScript, Pinia, Tailwind, Docker, Cloudflare Workers, DigitalOcean.</li></ul></div><div class="cv-sub"><div class="r1"><h4>Factory computer vision</h4><span class="when">Mar - Aug 2025</span></div><ul><li>Built an on-device computer-vision app on a Raspberry Pi that reads a machine’s display, checks each reading automatically and reports to the on-site operator.</li><li>Trained a small YOLO model to find each reading on the factory’s existing machine screen, then read it with EasyOCR.</li><li>Raspberry Pi 5, Python, PyTorch, OpenCV, YOLO, EasyOCR.</li></ul></div></div><div class="cv-role"><div class="r1"><h3>Full Stack Developer, Hivelocity</h3><span class="when">Jul 2021 - Mar 2024</span></div><div class="where">Tokyo, Japan / remote</div><ul><li>Built and maintained two product lines for a Japanese entertainment-tech company.</li><li>Developed and extended the <span class="nb">EC-CUBE</span> platform behind music artists’ fan-club stores: merchandise, memberships and gacha.</li><li>Built the sites for IP-licensed pop-up cafés (Hello Kitty and similar) on WordPress and WooCommerce.</li><li>Built the sales reporting and the data imports the business ran on.</li></ul></div><div class="cv-role"><div class="r1"><h3>Full Stack Engineer (Contract), SamePage Inc.</h3><span class="when">Nov 2020 - Jun 2021</span></div><div class="where">Tokyo, Japan / remote</div><ul><li>Customized and built e-commerce websites on <span class="nb">EC-CUBE</span> for the company’s clients, as an embedded member of a Japanese-speaking team.</li></ul></div><div class="cv-role"><div class="r1"><h3>Developer, Omise</h3><span class="when">Apr 2015 - Aug 2020</span></div><div class="where">Bangkok, Thailand</div><ul><li>Built and maintained the public payment plugins and libraries for WooCommerce, Magento, OpenCart, PrestaShop, <span class="nb">EC-CUBE</span> and PHP.</li><li>Supported merchants directly on integration issues.</li></ul></div><div class="cv-role"><div class="r1"><h3>Earlier roles</h3><span class="when">Dec 2011 - Mar 2015</span></div><div class="where">Bangkok, Thailand</div><ul><li>Web developer and PHP programmer at VBT Communications, Diversition, Cubic Creative and OneCallAsia. Built a provident fund module for Siam Commercial Bank.</li></ul></div></div><div class="cv-track"><p class="cv-track-name">Founder track</p><div class="cv-role"><div class="r1"><h3>Founder &amp; Managing Director, YATTA! Idol Management</h3><span class="when">May 2021 - Dec 2024</span></div><div class="where">Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam</div><ul><li>Founded an entertainment company and produced END OF IDOL, a seven-member Vietnamese idol group. Composed its three songs, about resilience, self-worth and self-determination, and built the group’s identity around them.</li><li>Carried a standing team of eleven at full size: seven members, three teachers and one assistant, plus choreographers, lyricists, makeup and media crews per event.</li><li>Did the work of every department I couldn’t afford to hire: designed the shows, cut the video, shot the photos, ran the social accounts and negotiated the brand deals.</li></ul></div><div class="cv-role"><div class="r1"><h3>Founder, Morei: matching actors and models with agencies</h3><span class="when">2024</span></div><div class="where">Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam</div><ul><li>Designed and built a platform that matches actors to casting work.</li><li>Reached out to hundreds of actors and to entertainment job agencies, pitched and sold the platform, onboarded both sides, matched talent to jobs, and handled the work between agencies and talent.</li><li>Pitched Morei at FORTEC 2024, La French Tech Vietnam’s technology forum in Ho Chi Minh City.</li></ul></div></div><div class="cv-track"><p class="cv-track-name">Personal &amp; AI project track</p><div class="cv-role"><div class="r1"><h3>Lucy, personal AI operating system</h3><span class="when">Jul 2026 - Present</span></div><ul><li>Designed the workflow, policies, architecture and tools that run a team of AI agents, built on Claude Code.</li><li>I run my day-to-day production work and life management on it.</li></ul></div></div></section>
            <section class="cv-block"><p class="label">Open source (2015-2020)</p><div class="cv-cols"><p class="cv-line"><b>omise-woocommerce</b>: #1 all-time contributor. 2,000+ active installs.</p><p class="cv-line"><b>omise-magento</b>: #2 all-time contributor.</p><p class="cv-line"><b>omise-opencart</b>: #1 all-time contributor.</p><p class="cv-line"><b>omise-php</b>: #2 all-time contributor.</p></div><p class="cv-line cv-note">Contributed as <a href="https://github.com/guzzilar">github.com/guzzilar</a>, my earlier GitHub account.</p></section>
      <section class="cv-block"><p class="label">Skills</p><div class="cv-cols"><p class="cv-line"><b>AI:</b> Claude Code, Codex, agentic workflow, multi-agent orchestration &amp; governance policies, computer vision</p><p class="cv-line"><b>Languages:</b> PHP, TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, SQL</p><p class="cv-line"><b>Back end:</b> Laravel, REST APIs, queues and background jobs, Node.js</p><p class="cv-line"><b>Front end:</b> Nuxt, Vue, Next.js, React, Pinia, Tailwind</p><p class="cv-line"><b>Payments and commerce:</b> payment gateway integration, prepaid wallets and ledgers, WooCommerce, Magento, OpenCart, PrestaShop, <span class="nb">EC-CUBE</span>, WordPress</p><p class="cv-line"><b>Data and platforms:</b> PostgreSQL, MySQL, LINE LIFF, Docker, Cloudflare Workers, AWS, DigitalOcean, Git, Raspberry Pi</p><p class="cv-line"><b>Industries:</b> payments, e-commerce, online marketing, entertainment</p><p class="cv-line"><b>Also coded in:</b> Ruby (Rails), Go (Gin), Swift (iOS)</p></div></section>
      <section class="cv-block"><p class="label">Languages</p><p class="cv-line">English (fluent) / Thai (native) / Vietnamese (conversational) / Japanese (conversational)</p></section>
    </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <script>
    import "../scripts/engineering/cv-print";
  </script>
</EngineeringLayout>
